"Bill Wayne" <HWayne@gmail.com> writes:
> Is there any general advice anybody has about the midgame? Nethack has
> sucked up a huge portion of my time, so I'd like to get better at it.

I think the most important thing to learn when you're starting to
consistently get to the midgame is that you need to be risk-averse.
If something has (or leads to) lethal consequences one time out of a
hundred, then that's not something you do, ever, unless by so doing
you can eliminate a greater risk.

Over the course of the thousands of such decisions in a typical game,
any risk of a game-ending outcome is too much.

Another related thing is learning to think ahead. You need to start
keeping a mental catalogue of problems you expect and resources needed
to counter them. (I'm at a Plvl+Dlvl where I can see cockatrices. Do I
have my Lizard Onna Stick(tm) in main inventory? Acid blob? Can I
safely pray?)

Build toward an ascension kit. Manage stashes. Keep track of
non-mobile resources like altars and special-level entrances.

But mostly it's about care, discipline and thinking before you press
the key.


